#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d5966ea-c284-532e-82fa-1c20c407ab53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{3}=3 \\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} + 15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693430} {:answer/id #uuid "40fe1bdf-f6e5-537e-94e7-1c761fdd9324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{3}=6 \\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} + 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693431} {:answer/id #uuid "619b43b1-7570-5b21-ba71-298ca53223d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{3}=3 \\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693437} {:answer/id #uuid "83a205d1-93fe-5813-8e5e-0449f423b502" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{3}=- 6 \\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} + 32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693440} {:answer/id #uuid "f6247efa-dbd5-521f-8e0d-b4919df21fbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^{3}=3 \\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} - 11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693458}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693430} :answer-field/id #uuid "fad3e21f-1b36-51be-8913-61b60c3f1347" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f3d82ec0-2d52-503e-a343-bc32995532d3" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2 \\left(x + 1\\right)}{y^{2}}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(1)=3.$ Assume that $y>0.$" :question/worked-solution "Separate the variables and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\left(2 x + 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\int \\left(2 x + 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{y^{3}}{3} &=\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the initial condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 &=4+C \\\\ C &=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y^{3}}{3} &=\\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} + 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by $3$ to obtain the requested relation:\n\n$$\ny^{3}=3 \\left(x + 1\\right)^{2} + 15\n$$\n\nThis is the local particular solution on the connected interval through the initial point where the original equation is defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4afd5ad7-8c5a-5307-ad22-64c432dc5f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- \\frac{4 \\tan{\\left(7 x - 14 \\right)}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693464}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186693464} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b6dfdb0-24a1-5c9a-b5e7-c5f987ad28d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186693463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "814f9b40-c597-5f52-863b-27537e10cfa4" :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=- \\frac{\\sec^{2}{\\left(7 x - 14 \\right)}}{\\sec^{2}{\\left(4 y \\right)}}\n$$\n\nthat satisfies $y(2)=0.$ Assume that $-\\pi/8<y<\\pi/8.$\n\n$\\tan{\\left(4 y \\right)}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Separate the variables and integrate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sec^{2}{\\left(4 y \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=- \\sec^{2}{\\left(7 x - 14 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\int \\sec^{2}{\\left(4 y \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}y &=\\int - \\sec^{2}{\\left(7 x - 14 \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ \\frac{\\tan{\\left(4 y \\right)}}{4} &=- \\frac{\\tan{\\left(7 x - 14 \\right)}}{7}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the initial condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 &=0+C \\\\ C &=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstitute this constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\tan{\\left(4 y \\right)}}{4} &=- \\frac{\\tan{\\left(7 x - 14 \\right)}}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiply both sides by $4$ to obtain the requested relation:\n\n$$\n\\tan{\\left(4 y \\right)}=- \\frac{4 \\tan{\\left(7 x - 14 \\right)}}{7}\n$$\n\nThis is the local particular solution on the connected interval through the initial point where the original equation is defined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6299f072-9ed7-5551-a10c-63ca9a9e0a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(2x)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697159} {:answer/id #uuid "8c317928-bbbb-5b46-a97f-38516707afa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2(2x+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697160} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8d0e3e-86ba-5ca8-a071-4abe73324087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(2x+1)^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697161} {:answer/id #uuid "b55753b5-2d5f-5e5e-8179-950befc2864c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6(2x+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697164} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaa5507-673b-5495-9c4e-f5a9d3758829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3(2x+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697168}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697164} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb1b353-f6ca-5091-82a4-46c3c308f2e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "16ea0705-2342-5b78-944f-84d5268fd2eb" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(2x+1)^3$, find $f'(x)$.\n\nUse the decomposition $g(x)=2x+1$ and $F(u)=u^3$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$. Recall that $f'(x)=F'(g(x))g'(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the outer and inner functions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF'(u)&=3u^2, \\\\\ng'(x)&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule multiplies the outer derivative, evaluated at the unchanged inner expression, by the inner derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=F'(g(x))g'(x) \\\\\n&=3(2x+1)^2\\cdot 2 \\\\\n&=6(2x+1)^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e61cb88-4009-5620-84fc-a9080a4da648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697157}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697157} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c66ad95-0e1a-5f4f-b282-666f579aebe1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9bc757c8-8f4c-5efa-890c-24f6558197c9" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{x^2-3x+3}}$, complete the expression for $f'(x)$ by entering the missing factor.\n\n$f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{(x^2-3x+3)^{3/2}}\\,($ {{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=x^2-3x+3$ and rewrite the outer function as $F(u)=2u^{-1/2}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiate the outer and inner functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF'(u)&=2\\left(-\\frac12\\right)u^{-3/2}=-u^{-3/2}, \\\\\ng'(x)&=2x-3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=F'(g(x))g'(x) \\\\\n&=-(x^2-3x+3)^{-3/2}(2x-3) \\\\\n&=\\frac{3-2x}{(x^2-3x+3)^{3/2}} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{(x^2-3x+3)^{3/2}}(3-2x).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing factor is $3-2x$. It includes both the inner derivative and the outer derivative's factor of $-1$.\n\nSince $x^2-3x+3=(x-\\frac32)^2+\\frac34>0$, this derivative is defined for every real $x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd39cb58-6343-57f1-aaba-008b64577b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-8(3-2x)^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697165}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697165} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f18178-7a19-5ada-8f9e-6db3f7e933b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b2e6e7b9-4715-540f-bb2f-b216b11323a6" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(3-2x)^4$, find $f'(x)$.\n\n$f'(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=3-2x$ and $F(u)=u^4$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiate each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF'(u)&=4u^3, \\\\\ng'(x)&=-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the chain rule and substitute $g(x)=3-2x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=F'(g(x))g'(x) \\\\\n&=4(3-2x)^3\\cdot(-2) \\\\\n&=-8(3-2x)^3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inner derivative supplies the negative sign; the inner expression itself stays $3-2x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698030 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67691eaf-b00e-54c2-89e3-3418966ba0e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 15 \\left(9 - 5 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698035} {:answer/id #uuid "68a16847-1298-5640-8682-a4d63c941720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\left(9 - 10 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698036} {:answer/id #uuid "69eb4219-ab76-5d58-8b39-4d279478a2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 5 \\left(9 - 5 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698037} {:answer/id #uuid "8c9947f1-2ef7-5b37-940d-bf81932542cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 15 \\left(9 - 10 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698043} {:answer/id #uuid "8da642bf-0aa8-5867-b10e-d9b97d74f7e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\left(9 - 5 x\\right)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698044}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698035} :answer-field/id #uuid "120d00f6-258d-53b5-ba58-fc5c76a41e66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2f3f583e-3609-5938-ab2c-9679cf2c703c" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(9 - 5 x\\right)^{3}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=9 - 5 x$ and $F(g)=g^{3}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=3 g^{2}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(3 \\left(9 - 5 x\\right)^{2}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-5\\right) \\\\ &=- 15 \\left(9 - 5 x\\right)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698031 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f43c25-25a1-5f15-be5e-fa7272043524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(54 \\left(9 x - 11\\right)^{5})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698024} {:answer/id #uuid "cead8dc0-12a5-59dc-811f-f07341ac0cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "54 \\left(9 x - 11\\right)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698048}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698048} :answer-field/id #uuid "6db4dc76-49a1-51b1-bcca-38814b4c5021" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4d9ef932-f18f-5be6-97ae-cb72686349cc" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(9 x - 11\\right)^{6}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=9 x - 11$ and $F(g)=g^{6}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=6 g^{5}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(6 \\left(9 x - 11\\right)^{5}\\right)\\cdot\\left(9\\right) \\\\ &=54 \\left(9 x - 11\\right)^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078ac3ae-f526-5351-b317-b05f60c2f99f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 8 \\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698023} {:answer/id #uuid "60dfa102-7a8e-57dc-b906-5558374df8b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 13 \\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698034} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8b73ec-cd60-595a-99ce-bc10d2174f42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 45 \\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698039} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c0e603-0498-55e3-aa47-5361a6335d35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 40 \\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698046} {:answer/id #uuid "c9c0fb2f-9630-572a-8cc2-1907f2de1da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 39 \\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698047}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698046} :answer-field/id #uuid "59d3d389-b546-51cd-92db-e0f9d95220c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698032}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7f492990-8d20-538e-b5c5-63a967568bd4" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{8}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=1 - 5 x$ and $F(g)=g^{8}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=8 g^{7}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(8 \\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{7}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-5\\right) \\\\ &=- 40 \\left(1 - 5 x\\right)^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5db149b3-9250-5cc6-8ee0-8cdaf81c7ee3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(- 30 \\left(8 - 6 x\\right)^{4})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698033} {:answer/id #uuid "9b97600c-ca9f-570c-a1b2-d54332bf6521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 30 \\left(8 - 6 x\\right)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698045}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698045} :answer-field/id #uuid "833c8ba4-4ad9-521b-95b3-7b36fc66c363" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8c466867-7e45-5195-8c17-0cb61679673c" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(8 - 6 x\\right)^{5}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$\n\n$f^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=8 - 6 x$ and $F(g)=g^{5}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=5 g^{4}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(5 \\left(8 - 6 x\\right)^{4}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-6\\right) \\\\ &=- 30 \\left(8 - 6 x\\right)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00ecca7a-0ca6-50a8-8215-c0b2e7d792f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 8 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698022} {:answer/id #uuid "1661f7cb-a47c-5177-b0e9-cfd39fe0900b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 16 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698026} {:answer/id #uuid "17d63a17-5737-5b1b-bac5-56d57f676a6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 14 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698027} {:answer/id #uuid "2477220f-fa13-533d-9869-05e65d9ee658" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 17 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698029} {:answer/id #uuid "da30ae38-a63c-5d6b-90d4-51ad8e4f5340" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "- 2 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698049}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186698026} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bb14453-3255-52fe-9245-b137f7000c50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186698028}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e38650e7-313f-5ee5-8a23-5355ea2ec56b" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{8}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=- 2 x - 2$ and $F(g)=g^{8}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} F^{\\prime}(g)&=8 g^{7}, \\\\ g^{\\prime}(x)&=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} f^{\\prime}(x)&=F^{\\prime}(g(x))\\cdot g^{\\prime}(x) \\\\ &=\\left(8 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{7}\\right)\\cdot\\left(-2\\right) \\\\ &=- 16 \\left(- 2 x - 2\\right)^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bc56bb8-3469-5e28-8f73-4057eaf34b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y=e^x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700094} {:answer/id #uuid "371c9f76-1ae1-5dee-afb0-3178347fbb0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=e^x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700097} {:answer/id #uuid "76c04fd7-041c-5ec1-91c8-477d878b6d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y=e^x+\\frac{x^2}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700101} {:answer/id #uuid "97cbb4f5-2f1c-573f-9bed-32107929cbaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y=e^x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700106} {:answer/id #uuid "f329da44-ddb8-5096-836b-5f3b407468ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y=e^x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700112}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700094} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f120867-036a-5d27-a28f-292e2e99fa56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "16211115-7e40-5dd4-bd44-b6f360bfaf20" :question/problem "Find the general solution in implicit form to\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{x-y}+e^{-y}.\n$$\n\nFirst factor the right-hand side to separate the variables, then integrate. In the choices, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "The two terms share a factor $e^{-y}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=e^{-y}(e^x+1)\\\\e^y\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=e^x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $e^y$ is never zero, this separation loses no solutions. Integrate each side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int e^y\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\int(e^x+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\e^y&=e^x+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the required implicit form. It defines real solutions on intervals where $e^x+x+C>0$. Differentiating gives $e^y y\\prime=e^x+1$; division by $e^y$ recovers the original equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "363beded-81ac-5d19-9148-0c372b3c3a62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y+y=e^x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700096} {:answer/id #uuid "7933e072-ea91-541c-8865-809fb6b0540e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y+y=e^x+\\frac{x^2}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700102} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f018af-4300-5c5e-b574-61d499a302d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y+y=e^x-\\frac{x^2}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700107} {:answer/id #uuid "b8aff57b-85be-5854-a0c8-5f7d359e7f7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y-y=e^x-\\frac{x^2}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700108} {:answer/id #uuid "c2bb3da2-50db-5627-b57d-c1e48bbe0834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y=e^x-\\frac{x^2}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700109}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700107} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bfe0073-964d-5f4f-8c96-245046015901" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "37bbda0c-7912-5120-8451-33cf7ffbedbf" :question/problem "Find the general solution in implicit form to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}+e^{-y}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{x-y}-xe^{-y}.\n$$\n\nIn the choices, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Collect the derivative terms, factor the right-hand side, and multiply through by $e^y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+e^{-y})\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=e^{-y}(e^x-x)\\\\(e^y+1)\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=e^x-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe variables are now separated. Integrate both terms on each side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int(e^y+1)\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\int(e^x-x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\e^y+y&=e^x-\\frac{x^2}{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis relation is already the general solution in implicit form; solving for $y$ is unnecessary. No solutions were lost: $e^y>0$ and $e^y+1>0$ for every real $y$. The function $e^y+y$ is strictly increasing with range $\\mathbb{R}$, so each real $C$ defines a unique real branch for all real $x$. Differentiating yields $(e^y+1)y\\prime=e^x-x$; multiplying by $e^{-y}$ recovers the original equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1496d332-e266-5637-a9c7-8315946d9853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^2=-4x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700092} {:answer/id #uuid "22918177-ff1a-5312-9d6f-920439268600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^2=2x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700095} {:answer/id #uuid "5abc0e48-42d7-5592-8e3f-2703639006b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^2=4x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700100} {:answer/id #uuid "89791f31-050f-5ba4-a4f0-65a64696262c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y=2x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700104} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b848f8-cba1-5967-9bac-6b077b389a6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^2=4x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700110}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700100} :answer-field/id #uuid "db59e432-82ce-5bdc-809a-f9083a03f310" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8fb7a80e-fc00-571f-96af-0fe365867e21" :question/problem "Find the general solution in implicit form to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{4x}{y}.\n$$\n\nWork on an interval where $y\\ne 0$. In the choices, $C$ is an arbitrary constant." :question/worked-solution "Multiply by $y$ to separate the variables:\n\n$$\ny\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4x.\n$$\n\nIntegrate, using $\\mathrm{d}y=y\\prime\\,\\mathrm{d}x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y\\,\\mathrm{d}y&=\\int 4x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\\\frac{y^2}{2}&=2x^2+K\\\\y^2&=4x^2+2K.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRenaming $2K$ as $C$, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\ny^2=4x^2+C.\n$$\n\nUse a branch on which $y\\ne0$, as required by the original equation. Differentiating gives $2y y\\prime=8x$, hence $y\\prime=4x/y$. There is no need to isolate $y$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700257 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27819427-4ac3-589d-861c-217ecf9d4c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^3\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700255} {:answer/id #uuid "8fb24d18-32fa-5267-9bca-f55ed9facda8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{y^3}{x^2}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700262} {:answer/id #uuid "92328c9f-9019-5909-aab6-b619eac37cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x^2}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{y^3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700264} {:answer/id #uuid "a11447fd-0e4b-58b0-9ec7-8f98927f95e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "y^3\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700265} {:answer/id #uuid "f557a574-7290-56e1-9ebe-93d189161bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^3}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=x^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700272}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700255} :answer-field/id #uuid "727d5644-2760-5526-95c0-9a965c5dc27e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30cc8aba-5f7d-5972-bde7-0d6ad531ec45" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation. Assume $x>0$ and $y>0$.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{x^2}{y^3}\n$$\n\nChoose an equivalent equation in the form $A(y)\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=B(x)$, where $A(y)$ depends only on $y$ and $B(x)$ depends only on $x$." :question/worked-solution "The right-hand side is already a product of an $x$-only factor and a $y$-only factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=x^2\\cdot\\frac{1}{y^3}.\n$$\n\nSince $y>0$, multiply both sides by $y^3$ to obtain\n\n$$\ny^3\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=x^2.\n$$\n\nThe multiplier of the derivative depends only on $y$, and the right-hand side depends only on $x$. Equations with an $x$-dependent multiplier of the derivative do not have the requested form, even when they are equivalent to the original equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700268 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28c1a714-61aa-5d5f-8efd-9e4426900b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^y\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700256} {:answer/id #uuid "65df1fc4-5ef8-5e8a-b3e9-2739fad1d21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{-y}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700259} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7a7347-bcdb-5d60-b1dd-809f8f764900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700267} {:answer/id #uuid "c72c6f6f-84fb-5df1-a6a0-865d0e66d116" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{-y}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700269} {:answer/id #uuid "e3780057-e76e-52a5-b462-1ecd2409943c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700271}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700256} :answer-field/id #uuid "107c795a-50b2-5b71-80fa-cabef5296e0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700252}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c151956e-c425-5beb-bc27-2e419d91ecda" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation. Assume $x$ and $y$ are real.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{2x-y}\n$$\n\nChoose an equivalent equation in the form $A(y)\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=B(x)$, where $A(y)$ depends only on $y$ and $B(x)$ depends only on $x$." :question/worked-solution "Use the exponent law $e^{a-b}=e^a e^{-b}$ to expose the two factors:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{2x-y}=e^{2x}\\cdot e^{-y}.\n$$\n\nThe $y$-only factor is $e^{-y}$. Its reciprocal is $e^y$, which is defined for every real $y$. Multiplying both sides by $e^y$ gives\n\n$$\ne^y\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=e^{2x}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying instead by $e^{-2x}$ gives an equivalent equation, but its derivative multiplier depends on $x$, so it is not the requested separated form."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1221f249-62c8-5cdf-9145-f4fbd0e4795b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(y^2+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3x+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700253} {:answer/id #uuid "60819443-1805-5915-8d4f-7f87d5f2fd9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(y^2+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700258} {:answer/id #uuid "79a18bfd-da83-517f-b952-22614bc75ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y^2+3}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700261} {:answer/id #uuid "903091ff-cee2-53c9-8d08-a4b374f5337d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(y^2+2)\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3x+3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700263} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d72c97-9ede-5158-bd43-e3c43213c3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(y^2+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{3x+2}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700266}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700258} :answer-field/id #uuid "218ba3d7-7035-5bbe-82e7-5f89409de700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "cc5a1273-5dc7-5e11-84b3-66860d1de773" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation. Assume $x>0$ and $y$ is real.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3xy^2+9x+2y^2+6}\n$$\n\nChoose an equivalent equation in the form $A(y)\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=B(x)$, where $A(y)$ depends only on $y$ and $B(x)$ depends only on $x$." :question/worked-solution "First factor the denominator by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3xy^2+9x+2y^2+6&=3x(y^2+3)+2(y^2+3)\\\\&=(3x+2)(y^2+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis reveals an $x$-only factor and a $y$-only factor:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{(3x+2)(y^2+3)}=\\frac{2x}{3x+2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{y^2+3}.\n$$\n\nSince $y^2+3>0$, multiply both sides by this factor:\n\n$$\n(y^2+3)\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{3x+2}.\n$$\n\nThe denominator $3x+2$ is nonzero because $x>0$. The variables are now separated. Expanding $(3x+2)(y^2+3)$ recovers all four terms in the original denominator; replacing either factor by a different sum changes the equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700330 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d408795-750d-5fea-94c5-e67dfaf90aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x-5^x\\ln 5+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700331} {:answer/id #uuid "4f8cb77a-bb89-5549-89e8-79bc984f2a9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700335} {:answer/id #uuid "58a5f3f5-37a9-58cb-a102-516ff6fca8ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x-\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700336} {:answer/id #uuid "8ae34f9a-398a-50d3-9a64-36e9622e36ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3x}-\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700341} {:answer/id #uuid "a66ed43a-a4c0-5250-bdf2-7bac8a492fc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x-\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+2x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700344}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700336} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9e7f0bf-910b-55d2-94ea-b3254d648bcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700350}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0b41fc15-0419-5dab-9326-497b409c7f92" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left(3e^x-5^x+2x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Integrate term by term, keeping the minus sign on the general-base exponential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\int (3e^x-5^x+2x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=3\\int e^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x-\\int 5^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x+2\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=3e^x-\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+2\\left(\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right)+C \\\\\n&=3e^x-\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the exponential rules for the first two terms and the power rule for $x$. Include one arbitrary constant in the final sum."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700334 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58d6d1b4-566d-5f6c-baf8-c28051d31229" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700337} {:answer/id #uuid "ac695a0a-5172-59f8-bdd9-2cc26593dd01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x\\ln 5+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700345} {:answer/id #uuid "bb8e483c-0053-583c-b11a-0c40c12d1e98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x-\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700346} {:answer/id #uuid "dc721f58-3ab1-51e3-8b51-ac399aa6150a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700348} {:answer/id #uuid "dfebba05-5384-525a-9f3e-82f8cfd4a06b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x}{\\ln 5}+2x^2+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700349}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700348} :answer-field/id #uuid "a26287ea-d380-533c-a929-8a84c30df483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4a320810-263a-5959-8c71-4ea40b8f7529" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left(3e^x-\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x+2x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Apply the sum and constant factor rules, then integrate each term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\int \\left(3e^x-\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x+2x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=3\\int e^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x-\\int \\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x+2\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=3e^x-\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)}+x^2+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe base is $1/5$, so the denominator is its logarithm. Simplify it using\n\n$$\n\\ln\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)=\\ln 1-\\ln 5=-\\ln 5.\n$$\n\nThe subtraction sign and the negative denominator cancel:\n\n$$\n3e^x-\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x}{-\\ln 5}+x^2+C\n=3e^x+\\frac{\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)^x}{\\ln 5}+x^2+C.\n$$\n\nThus the reciprocal-base term has a positive coefficient in the antiderivative, even though it is subtracted in the integrand."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700347 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15ca3ad1-f1d5-5483-89a3-1b342d5b9837" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700332} {:answer/id #uuid "5e2fad4e-02f1-571b-9e5e-151070543d52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+5^x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700338} {:answer/id #uuid "74d81977-ff24-5441-a79d-152e06391d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+\\frac{x^5}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700339} {:answer/id #uuid "7543c192-734d-5c30-bb01-51a90d6354dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{3x}+\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700340} {:answer/id #uuid "a394f013-88dc-59a5-bf49-a0ab13afba15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3e^x+5^x\\ln 5+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700343}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700332} :answer-field/id #uuid "19f98875-0f49-5f80-a65a-36e3c9df2199" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c06582f3-4466-5fb9-ac90-292decce7fa6" :question/problem "Calculate\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left(3e^x+5^x\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Apply the sum rule and take the constant factor outside the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int (3e^x+5^x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n&=3\\int e^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int 5^x\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\\n&=3e^x+\\frac{5^x}{\\ln 5}+C.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe integral of $e^x$ is $e^x$, while the integral of $a^x$ is $a^x/\\ln a$ for $a>0$ and $a\\ne 1$. The constant $C$ accounts for all antiderivatives."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87a9fa39-6763-5d3a-b23a-9acc33d33465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700374} {:answer/id #uuid "e070a7ab-83c0-5cb8-9b6a-21d0bbfcd45a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700375} {:answer/id #uuid "f5fd3d1e-b86e-50e6-8f30-7119c1471cb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700376} {:answer/id #uuid "fa63e1d4-df52-56a3-8e0d-d2ae1cee77d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3+{y}^{4}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x+2}{5x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700377} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8cc52c-8b62-5491-9bf4-26a449ead9bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(3+{y}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700374} :answer-field/id #uuid "7744e3ea-11f5-5c3b-adca-25b3614800ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7aa241e4-4c56-559c-8980-16301c4a85c5" :question/problem "Separate the variables in the following differential equation: \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{6x+2x{y}^{4}+6+2{y}^{4}}\n$$\n\nWork on an open domain where all displayed expressions are defined and the dependent-variable factor is nonzero. Choose an equivalent equation in the form $A(y)\\, \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=B(x)$, with a multiplier depending only on $y$ and a right-hand side depending only on $x$." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is *separable* if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x)g(y).\n$$\n\nIf an equation is separable, we say that the variables are *separated* when it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{g(y)}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=h(x).\n$$\n\nNotice that our differential equation is separable since it can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5x}{(2x+2)(3+{y}^{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x}{2x+2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3+{y}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we separate the variables as follows:\n\n$$\n(3+{y}^{4})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5x}{2x+2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d41270-1bf8-596b-8c26-537b55f24f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=- x^{2} + 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700383} {:answer/id #uuid "43b99790-f9e3-51c2-b5f7-cd318f2e7669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=x^{2} + 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700387} {:answer/id #uuid "615607ba-d978-5e35-ae3e-3992fc8b4da4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=- x^{2} - 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700393} {:answer/id #uuid "83185a9a-f331-5de9-a404-d54f89e7f243" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=x^{2} - 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700397} {:answer/id #uuid "f59b5182-91d5-5b1d-89b3-d39eaa944009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700412}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700387} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7315222-d873-53b5-b4a3-471cb057db19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5d3cdaf5-2350-5894-bb9f-940cfcd7675c" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 e^{- y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2 x e^{- y} + 2 e^{x - y}.$" :question/worked-solution "Collect the derivative terms, then multiply both sides by $e^y$ to separate the variables.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1 + 2 e^{- y})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 x e^{- y} + 2 e^{x - y} \\\\ (e^{y} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2 x + 2 e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate both sides term by term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y} + 2)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2 x + 2 e^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 y + e^{y} & =x^{2} + 2 e^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\n2 y + e^{y}=x^{2} + 2 e^{x}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700394 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03dc8970-b129-57ca-ad97-7f488c102267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y}=- \\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700380} {:answer/id #uuid "17dfbd92-15cc-5bc7-b86b-beeb7ac2132c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700384} {:answer/id #uuid "325626bc-b9cc-5fec-9eeb-3247cb89658d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700386} {:answer/id #uuid "720390e0-6253-5106-8f56-165a4b635f2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=- \\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700395} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b2b0cc-4136-575f-93c7-1a6f3c44862e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=- x - 2 e^{x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700401}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700395} :answer-field/id #uuid "728f45c2-f20b-50dd-abde-daf0becc8282" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6c1d8077-34df-559b-b678-b4720f491853" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 e^{- y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- x e^{- y} - 2 e^{x - y}.$" :question/worked-solution "Collect the derivative terms, then multiply both sides by $e^y$ to separate the variables.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1 + 2 e^{- y})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- x e^{- y} - 2 e^{x - y} \\\\ (e^{y} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- x - 2 e^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate both sides term by term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y} + 2)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (- x - 2 e^{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2 y + e^{y} & =- \\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 2 e^{x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution in implicit form is\n\n$$\n2 y + e^{y}=- \\frac{x^{2}}{2} - 2 e^{x}+C.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "132d4f66-fc83-5400-8a5f-e5fd14a389da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=\\frac{x^{2}}{2} - \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700381} {:answer/id #uuid "143b2b68-3f7c-5eca-affb-8152be3523af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=- x + \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700382} {:answer/id #uuid "d6257211-55a4-5ada-96e9-f9915b6e6ff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700405} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fcf4f8-f3de-5d25-9ed8-08444098b5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "e^{y}=- \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700409} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f6b7b9-ab07-5603-84ac-3d05da375d98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 y + e^{y}=- \\frac{x^{2}}{2} + \\frac{e^{2 x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700410}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186700410} :answer-field/id #uuid "5652a55f-11ae-5bb3-88e4-db16289763d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186700390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "88e2c01b-fb6b-5328-9a16-6305ee95c943" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2 e^{- y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=- x e^{- y} + e^{2 x - y}.$" :question/worked-solution "Collect the derivative terms, then multiply both sides by $e^y$ to separate the variables.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1 + 2 e^{- y})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- x e^{- y} + e^{2 x - y} \\\\ (e^{y} + 2)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =- x + e^{2 x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrate both sides term by term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (e^{y} + 2)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (-